# Redis Iris basics: settings. Copy this file to .env next to pyproject.toml, uncomment every
# name, and fill them in. marimo loads .env when the kernel starts. A variable already set in
# your shell wins over the file. Column 0 checks that every name is set, and the cells that
# read the environment wait for it. After you edit this file, restart the kernel.
# Console: https://cloud.redis.io

# ---- Redis Search (the same database is where Context Retriever writes) ----
# Any Redis 8 with Search and JSON, local or Redis Cloud. Console: the database's Configuration
# page (Public endpoint) and its Security page (Default user password). Use rediss:// on a TLS database.
# REDIS_URL=redis://default:<password>@<host>:<port>

# ---- LangCache ----
# Console: the service's Connectivity page (URL and Cache ID). The API key is shown once, when
# the service is created. Use a service of your own: a cache is shared by everything that
# points at it.
# LANGCACHE_HOST=https://<region>.langcache.redis.io
# LANGCACHE_CACHE_ID=
# LANGCACHE_API_KEY=

# ---- Context Retriever (also needs REDIS_URL above) ----
# Console: the Context Retriever Admin keys page. A new key is shown once. The database must have
# Search and JSON and be reachable by the hosted service, which is given its password.
# CTX_ADMIN_KEY=
# Optional. The default suits Redis Cloud. The MCP address is read from the agent-key listing.
# CTX_API_URL=https://cloud.redis.io/context-surfaces

# ---- Agent Memory ----
# Console: the service's General settings page (Endpoint, with https://, and Store ID) and its
# API keys page. A new key is shown once.
# MEMORY_API_BASE_URL=https://<endpoint>
# MEMORY_STORE_ID=
# MEMORY_API_KEY=

# ---- LLM (the chats in the Search, LangCache, and Agent Memory columns) ----
# An OpenAI key when AI_MODEL in column 0 starts with gpt, an Anthropic key when it starts with claude,
# or a Google AI Studio key when it starts with gemini.
# LLM_API_KEY=
